SUMMARY:Screen Life: Finding Balance in a World Full of Screens
DESCRIPTION:We’re living in a world of technology designed to keep us hooked – and most of us are navigating the balance alone. \nScreen Life is a free\, two-hour workshop on building a healthier relationship with your phone. Held at the University of Toronto’s Schwartz Reisman Innovation Campus on College Street\, the morning brings together a curated group of practitioners on focus\, burnout\, relationships\, family\, and AI — grounded in research\, delivered without judgment. \nYou’ll take a personal assessment\, hear from practitioners  working on the front lines of digital wellness \, and leave with a personalized concrete plan built for your real life. \nYou’ll leave with: \n\nPractical ways to feel less overwhelmed by constant connectivity\nA personal framework for a more intentional relationship with technology\n\nOpen to anyone. No tech background required. Capacity is limited and registration is approval-based\, so don’t wait. \nHosted by Offline.now and the Schwartz Reisman Innovation Campus Ecosystem team at the University of Toronto\, as part of Toronto Tech Week 2026.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/screen-life-finding-balance-in-a-world-full-of-screens/
LOCATION:U of T: Schwartz Reisman Innovation Campus\, 108 College St\, Toronto\, ON M5G 0C6\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5G 0C6
CATEGORIES:Classes & Workshops,Fitness & Wellness,Talks & Panels
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/screen-life-finding-balance-in-a-world-full-of-screens.png
END:VEVENT
