SUMMARY:International Ceramic Art Fair (ICAF) 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Gardiner Museum presents the return of the International Ceramic Art Fair (ICAF)\, its biennial celebration of innovation and contemporary directions in ceramics\, running May 28 to August 16\, 2026. \nThis year\, ICAF is expanded significantly from a 10-day event to a 12-week exhibition and public program\, positioning the fair at the forefront of how ceramics is evolving across art\, design\, and emerging technologies. \nAt the heart of this year’s edition is the theme “the city and the commons\,” presenting ceramics as both material and method for examining how we live together in rapidly changing cities. From architecture to infrastructure\, ceramics shelter\, connect\, and ground us\, offering new ways to think about belonging\, resilience\, and shared space. \nThe fair invites audiences to engage with urgent questions shaping contemporary life: How do we nurture communal relationships amidst dramatic change? How can material intelligence inform how we navigate cosmopolitan living? And how might emerging ceramic technologies reshape our sense of home\, security\, and belonging?
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/international-ceramic-art-fair-icaf-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queens Park 3rd floor\, Toronto\, ON M5S 2C7\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 2C7
CATEGORIES:Art & Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/international-ceramic-art-fair-icaf-2026.png
END:VEVENT
