SUMMARY:Don Pyle's Rough Description book launch
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for the launch of \nRough Description: Love Letters and Ghost Stories from a Life in Music (ECW Press)\, Don Pyle’s memoirish new book. \nSlideshow/reading by Don Pyle\, followed by a conversation moderated by Damian Rogers. \nwith fabulous guest readers: \nChris Colohan \nKirby \nJason McBride \nTabatha Southey \nDoors 7pm\, starting 7:30pm \nThursday May 28 2026 \nStandard Time. 165 Geary Ave\, 2nd floor \nAdvance tickets $10 https://ra.co/events/2368611 \nwith any profit benefitting the Unison Fund\, providing Canadian musicians with counselling\, emergency financial support\, and other resources. unisonfund.ca \nDon Pyle is a Toronto artist\, working primarily in music\, sound\, photography and writing. Author of two books\, including Trouble In The Camera Club\, he’s released 15 albums\, has shot photos for the covers of numerous books and records\, and has scored music for feature films and TV series. \nTabatha Southey is a freelance writer who is based\, in Toronto. She/Her. Bylines in Globe and Mail\, Macleans\, Foreign Policy\, Elle Magazine\, National Post\, Toronto Life\, Explore Magazine and more. She is the author of three books. \nDamian Rogers is a writer\, editor\, creative writing teacher\, and tarot reader. She is the author of two poetry collections and the memoir An Alphabet for Joanna. \nJason McBride is a freelance writer and editor in Toronto. His biography of Kathy Acker — Eat Your Mind: The Radical Life and Work of Kathy Acker — was published in 2022. \nKIRBY is the author of She\, Poetry is Queer\, This Is Where I Get Off\, featured columnist at Send My Love to Anyone and publisher at knife | fork | book. Their latest\, Fairy\, comes out Spring 2027 from Palimpsest Press. \nChris Colohan is a singer in punk and hardcore bands from the early 90s to present and author of Negative Space\, No He Is Not Sleeping and the impending pandemic-era collection A Battered Tomorrow. \nRough Description was supported by the Toronto Arts Council\, and the Ontario Arts Council Recommender Grant program. \nthedonpyle.com
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/don-pyles-rough-description-book-launch/
LOCATION:165 Geary Avenue\, 165 Geary Ave\, Toronto\, ON M6H 2B8\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6H 2B8
CATEGORIES:2SLGBTQ+,Literature & Spoken Word
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/don-pyles-rough-description-book-launch.png
END:VEVENT
