SUMMARY:Angle Mort (Blindside)
DESCRIPTION:Diagnosed with a malignant retinal tumor at the age of two\, Stéphanie Morin-Robert had to have her left eye removed and now lives with an ocular prosthesis. In a candid\, energetic\, and humorous autobiographical account\, she recounts her childhood in Northern Ontario\, the advantages and challenges of her condition both within her family and at school\, and how\, during a ball game in which her glass eye was dislodged from its socket\, she eventually managed to overcome her fear of being different. \nA show about resilience and the joy of living. After performing Blindside around the world for nearly a decade\, Stéphanie Morin-Robert produced a French version\, Angle Mort. Not only does she continue to fully embrace her disability\, but she also happily reclaims her Francophone roots and her identity. \nALL PERFORMANCES ARE ENGLISH SURTITLED. YOU ALSO HAVE THE OPTION TO TRY ON OUR AUGMENTED REALITY GLASSES FOR A MORE IMMERSIVE SURTITLING EXPERIENCE. TOGGLE BETWEEN ENGLISH OR FRENCH. YOUR PREFERENCE! OF COURSE\, IT’S FREE OF CHARGE.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/angle-mort-blindside/
LOCATION:Canadian Stage (Berkeley Street Theatre)\, 26 Berkeley St\, Toronto\, ON M5A 2W3\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5A 2W3
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,Theatre & Opera
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/angle-mort-blindside-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
